STEP 3: The workflow
--------------------
mkdir -p ~/k8s-journey/.github/workflows
vi ~/k8s-journey/.github/workflows/myapp.yaml

name: myapp-ci
on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
    paths: ["myapp/**"]

permissions:
  contents: write

jobs:
  build-and-deploy:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
    - uses: actions/checkout@v4

    - uses: actions/setup-python@v5
      with:
        python-version: "3.12"

    - name: Test
      working-directory: myapp
      run: |
        pip install pytest flask
        pytest -q

    - name: Set image tag
      run: echo "TAG=$(git rev-parse --short HEAD)" >> $GITHUB_ENV

    - uses: docker/login-action@v3
      with:
        username: ${{ secrets.DOCKERHUB_USERNAME }}
        password: ${{ secrets.DOCKERHUB_TOKEN }}

    - uses: docker/build-push-action@v6
      with:
        context: myapp
        file: myapp/Containerfile
        push: true
        tags: ${{ secrets.DOCKERHUB_USERNAME }}/myapp:${{ env.TAG }}

    - name: Update dev overlay
      run: |
        curl -sL "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kubernetes-sigs/kustomize/master/hack/install_kustomize.sh" | bash
        cd week8/kustomize/overlays/dev
        ../../../../kustomize edit set image myapp=docker.io/${{ secrets.DOCKERHUB_USERNAME }}/myapp:${{ env.TAG }}
        cd -
        git config user.name "github-actions"
        git config user.email "github-actions@users.noreply.github.com"
        git add week8/kustomize/overlays/dev/kustomization.yaml
        git commit -m "deploy myapp ${{ env.TAG }} to dev [skip ci]"
        git push

(If your Dockerfile is named "Dockerfile", change the "file:" line.
The kustomize binary is downloaded into the repo root, hence the
relative path ../../../../kustomize.)

git add . && git commit -m "ci: build and deploy myapp" && git push


STEP 4: Trigger it
------------------
Change the message in myapp/app.py (e.g. "v5 via CI"), commit, push.
GitHub -> Actions: watch the run. Then:
  git pull                      # the bot's commit with the new tag
  grep -A2 newTag week8/kustomize/overlays/dev/kustomization.yaml
  argocd app get myapp-dev      # OutOfSync -> Synced
  k get pods -n kz-dev -o jsonpath='{.items[*].spec.containers[0].image}{"\n"}'
  k port-forward -n kz-dev svc/myapp 5000:80 &
  curl localhost:5000 ; kill %1


STEP 5: Break the pipeline on purpose
-------------------------------------
Remove the /ready route from app.py, push. The Test step fails, no
image is built, nothing is deployed. Restore it.


STEP 6: Promotion to prod by pull request
-----------------------------------------
Create an Argo CD Application myapp-prod for overlays/prod (copy
app-dev.yaml). To promote:
  git checkout -b promote-<sha>
  edit overlays/prod/kustomization.yaml newTag to the dev SHA
  git commit -am "promote <sha> to prod" && git push -u origin HEAD
Open a PR, review the diff, merge -> Argo CD deploys prod.


